Good idea but this seems needlessly complex. Probably it can grep for
lines that begin with subject:, pick the first one (presuambly that's
the subject header line, right?) and then read everything after it.

Same with detecting added. Probably it can `jj st maildir` and then use
awk to identify added ones and only print their names.

I'm not opposed to this I guess... there is something nice about doing
it all in jj I suppose. It just seems like it's doing a lot there that
could be done with more idiomatic shell script processing.
